  "query_preview": "period. Rain and storm chances are forecast to return \ncloser to normal values on Sunday and Monday (30-60%), with \nchances falling Tuesday onward as drier air aloft moves across the\npeninsula and helps limit some convective potential. The return \nof the high pressure overhead will allow for some warming across \neast central Florida through the extended period, with afternoon \nhighs near to slightly above normal in the low to mid 90s. Peak \nheat indices are overall anticipated to remain between 102-107F, \nthough there is a low chance of exceeding 108F in some spots, but \nconfidence remains low at this time. Will closely monitor. Muggy \nconditions will continue into the overnight hours each day, with \nlows remaining near normal.",
